<!-- HITO 2: 225 a. C. — Apolonio de Perga -->
<article class="lt-item" data-stage="origenes">
<div class="lt-node" aria-hidden="true"><br /></div>
<div class="lt-card">
<div class="lt-card-trigger" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="lt-hito-2" tabindex="0">
<div class="lt-card-header-info">
<div class="lt-meta-row"><span class="lt-year-badge">225 a. C.</span> <span class="lt-stage-tag">Orígenes remotos</span></div>
<h3 class="lt-card-title">Teoría de las secciones cónicas</h3>
<p class="lt-protagonist">Apolonio de Perga</p>
</div>
<span class="lt-chevron" aria-hidden="true"> <svg width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg> </span></div>
<div class="lt-card-collapse" id="lt-hito-2">
<div class="lt-card-collapse-inner">
<div class="lt-card-body">
<div class="lt-text-col">
<p class="lt-summary">En su tratado <em>Cónicas</em>, Apolonio estudió de forma sistemática la circunferencia, la elipse, la parábola y la hipérbola como intersecciones de un cono con distintos planos, estableciendo relaciones geométricas precisas entre magnitudes asociadas a cada punto de la curva.</p>
<div class="lt-key-idea"><strong>Idea clave:</strong> Las curvas se describen mediante proporciones geométricas entre segmentos, anticipando las futuras ecuaciones de segundo grado.</div>
</div>
<!-- Nota para el docente: Puedes sustituir el <svg> siguiente por tu propia etiqueta <img src="ruta-imagen.jpg" alt="..."> -->
<figure class="lt-figure">
<div class="lt-zoom-trigger" role="button" data-zoom-title="225 a. C. — Secciones cónicas de Apolonio" aria-label="Ampliar ilustración: Secciones cónicas" tabindex="0"><svg viewbox="0 0 360 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Doble cono cortado por planos mostrando circunferencia, elipse, parábola e hipérbola"> <defs> <lineargradient id="lt-bg-2" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"> <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#FFF7ED"></stop> <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#FFEDD5"></stop> </lineargradient> <lineargradient id="lt-cone-2" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0"> <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#FDBA74" stop-opacity="0.65"></stop> <stop offset="50%" stop-color="#FFF7ED" stop-opacity="0.9"></stop> <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#EA580C" stop-opacity="0.45"></stop> </lineargradient> </defs> <rect width="360" height="220" fill="url(#lt-bg-2)"></rect> <polygon points="110,110 55,28 165,28" fill="url(#lt-cone-2)" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.6"></polygon> <ellipse cx="110" cy="28" rx="55" ry="11" fill="#FFEDD5" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.4"></ellipse> <polygon points="110,110 50,192 170,192" fill="url(#lt-cone-2)" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.6"></polygon> <ellipse cx="110" cy="192" rx="60" ry="12" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.4"></ellipse> <line x1="110" y1="14" x2="110" y2="208" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3"></line> <ellipse cx="110" cy="54" rx="38" ry="8" fill="rgba(15,118,110,0.22)" stroke="#0F766E" stroke-width="2.2"></ellipse> <ellipse cx="110" cy="144" rx="28" ry="11" transform="rotate(-18 110 144)" fill="rgba(234,88,12,0.2)" stroke="#EA580C" stroke-width="2.2"></ellipse> <path d="M124 192 Q132 145 152 162" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="2.4"></path> <g transform="translate(200, 22)"> <rect x="0" y="0" width="142" height="176" rx="10" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#FED7AA" stroke-width="1.4"></rect> <circle cx="38" cy="40" r="18" fill="none" stroke="#0F766E" stroke-width="2.4"></circle> <text x="38" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" fill="#1E293B">Circunferencia</text> <ellipse cx="106" cy="40" rx="22" ry="13" transform="rotate(-15 106 40)" fill="none" stroke="#EA580C" stroke-width="2.4"></ellipse> <text x="106" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" fill="#1E293B">Elipse</text> <path d="M18 140 Q38 86 58 140" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="2.4"></path> <text x="38" y="160" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" fill="#1E293B">Parábola</text> <path d="M88 100 Q102 122 88 144 M124 100 Q110 122 124 144" fill="none" stroke="#0F766E" stroke-width="2.4"></path> <text x="106" y="160" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" fill="#1E293B">Hipérbola</text> </g> </svg> <span class="lt-zoom-badge">Ampliar</span></div>
<figcaption class="lt-figcaption"><strong>Secciones cónicas:</strong> planos cortando un doble cono generan las cuatro curvas clásicas.</figcaption>
